<!DOCTYPE html>
{# PDFShift native page header — the SLIM RUNNING HEAD (§7.1, variant A).

   WHAT THIS USED TO BE. The full gradient masthead, repeated at its full
   1.165in on every page of every report. §7.1 always wanted a full masthead on
   page 1 and a one-line running head after it, and that was never built,
   because the obvious way to build it does not work.

   WHY IT IS NOT DONE THE OBVIOUS WAY (D-103). "Running head from page 2" means
   `header.start_at = 2`, and "footer on every page" means
   `footer.start_at = 1`. PDFShift accepts that pair with a 200 and silently
   applies `max(header, footer)` to BOTH, so the footer disappears from page 1
   with no error — measured, four renders, marker-searched per page. Both
   `start_at` values therefore stay at 1 and nothing is asked to differ.

   HOW §7.1'S INTENT IS REACHED ANYWAY. The masthead moved OUT of this slot and
   into the document body (macros.report_masthead), where it is ordinary
   first-page content under CSS control. This slot now carries only the running
   head, which appears on page 1 too — above the masthead rather than instead of
   it. §7.1 asked for a full masthead on page 1, not for no head on page 1.

   THE BREATHING ROOM IS INSIDE THIS DOCUMENT, DELIBERATELY. PDFShift's
   `margin.top` is now 0. A CSS `padding-top` on the body would apply once, at
   the start of the flow, not after each page break — so continuation pages
   would start flush against the band. The white strip below the bar is part of
   the header's own reserved height, which makes it uniform on every page.

   IMPORTANT: PDFShift renders header/footer in a separate document context, so
   CSS custom properties from the main document do NOT resolve here. Colours are
   literal hex passed via context; the logo is base64-embedded before the call.
#}
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-family: 'Outfit', 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif;
    width: 8.5in;
  }
  .running-head {
    /* Solid header_bg, not the masthead's gradient. The masthead's gradient
       BEGINS at header_bg, so on page 1 this band and the block beneath it meet
       on the same colour and read as one piece rather than two. */
    background: {{ header_bg }};
    color: #ffffff;
    padding: 8px 25px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .rh-name {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }
  .rh-city {
    font-weight: 400;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
  .rh-meta {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    padding-left: 16px;
  }
  /* Part of the reserved height — see the note above. */
  .rh-gap { height: 10px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="running-head">
  <span class="rh-name">{{ report_title }}{% if city %} <span class="rh-city">— {{ city }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
  {% if total_count %}
  <span class="rh-meta">{{ total_count }} {{ report_title }}</span>
  {% endif %}
</div>
<div class="rh-gap"></div>
</body>
</html>
